-- ============================================================
-- Vocabulary extension: seed 88 concepts and map the 417
--
-- Approved after the QA pass. Additive and reversible; rollback at the foot.
-- Nothing is touched outside the taxonomy tables.
--
-- WHAT THE MAPPING IS. Unlike the first 2,242, these do NOT map by string
-- equality: a per-question descriptor is not a concept name. Instead the
-- descriptor-to-concept table below IS the approved artifact, and this file
-- applies it mechanically. Provenance is DETERMINISTIC rather than
-- DETERMINISTIC_EXACT for exactly that reason, and it is deliberately not
-- HUMAN_VALIDATED: the vocabulary and the clustering were reviewed, but not
-- each of 417 individual rows, and the status should not claim otherwise.
-- ============================================================

-- ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- 1. Rename the existing concept, preserving its ID
--
-- All six of its questions are respiratory: panting, nasal and tracheal
-- mucosal blood flow, and why panting does not produce alkalosis. Checked
-- programmatically before writing this: zero of the six lack respiratory
-- vocabulary in stem or explanation.
--
-- The ID does not change, its 6 existing mappings are untouched, and the
-- concepts_archive_rename trigger files "Thermoregulation" as a LEGACY_NAME
-- alias automatically. That is the rename lifecycle working as designed.
-- ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
UPDATE public.concepts
SET canonical_name = 'Respiratory Thermoregulation'
WHERE canonical_name = 'Thermoregulation';

